00:31:54.743 --> 00:31:57.750
Or is it a local movie theater?

00:31:57.750 --> 00:32:00.410
So bringing all of this
data into the cloud

00:32:00.410 --> 00:32:01.880
with your own data
would then allow

00:32:01.880 --> 00:32:04.540
you to do some very
interesting analytics.

00:32:04.540 --> 00:32:06.800
Do the machine learning on it.

00:32:06.800 --> 00:32:09.290
Do some visualizations
and make some insights

00:32:09.290 --> 00:32:11.318
into your customer operations.

00:32:13.950 --> 00:32:15.505
Similarly, internet
of things use

00:32:15.505 --> 00:32:17.630
cases is something we're
seeing a lot of excitement

00:32:17.630 --> 00:32:18.690
around right now.

00:32:18.690 --> 00:32:21.800
We have all these new
connected devices.

00:32:21.800 --> 00:32:27.440
Investing in GPS hardware for
a low-cost connected device,

00:32:27.440 --> 00:32:29.980
like a wearable,
might be prohibitive.

00:32:29.980 --> 00:32:34.550
Our geolocation API is one
of our lesser known APIs,

00:32:34.550 --> 00:32:36.090
but it is very powerful.

00:32:36.090 --> 00:32:40.790
We have a global database of
millions of Wi-Fi cell towers

00:32:40.790 --> 00:32:44.060
which if you have a device
that just has a Wi-Fi internet,

00:32:44.060 --> 00:32:47.840
you can query for those
nearby Wi-Fi hotspots,

00:32:47.840 --> 00:32:50.004
use our geolocation API to
get a real-time position

00:32:50.004 --> 00:32:51.170
of that device in the world.

00:32:56.570 --> 00:32:59.890
Another area that we're
seeing a lot of interest

00:32:59.890 --> 00:33:07.330
is around Google's capabilities
to standardize and validate

00:33:07.330 --> 00:33:09.130
and verify addresses.

00:33:09.130 --> 00:33:13.060
So we see this in a number of
different industries right now.

00:33:13.060 --> 00:33:16.480
So for example, you may have
used our address autocomplete

00:33:16.480 --> 00:33:18.340
service, where you
start typing an address

00:33:18.340 --> 00:33:20.256
and Google will provide
a list of suggestions.

00:33:20.256 --> 00:33:22.800
Well, it turns out that if
you incorporate that in, say,

00:33:22.800 --> 00:33:26.950
an e-commerce flow, for
example, an online store,

00:33:26.950 --> 00:33:29.410
using that as part of
your checkout process,

00:33:29.410 --> 00:33:33.160
you can decrease shopping cart
abandonment rate and increase

00:33:33.160 --> 00:33:36.370
conversion rates, by just
simplifying that checkout

00:33:36.370 --> 00:33:37.407
experience.

00:33:37.407 --> 00:33:39.490
Especially on mobile
devices, where people may not

00:33:39.490 --> 00:33:43.940
be wanting to sit there and
enter multiple address fields.

00:33:43.940 --> 00:33:47.710
It also decreases shipping
errors and delivery errors

00:33:47.710 --> 00:33:53.470
by having the assurance that
the address has been entered

00:33:53.470 --> 00:33:56.169
is correct and exists
within Google's database.

00:34:05.280 --> 00:34:07.100
So those are just a
few examples of how

00:34:07.100 --> 00:34:11.840
you can incorporate our APIs
in a real-life application.

